WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.870
- [Voiceover] Oxford
Dictionaries just announced

00:00:01.870 --> 00:00:03.589
their word of the year for 2015,

00:00:03.589 --> 00:00:06.175
which is the crying laughing emoji.

00:00:06.175 --> 00:00:08.425
Reporting that it makes up to 17% of all

00:00:08.425 --> 00:00:10.171
emoji use in the United States.

00:00:10.171 --> 00:00:13.706
I know what you're all thinking,
how is it not the eggplant?

00:00:13.706 --> 00:00:15.532
OK, we're going to go talk to some people

00:00:15.532 --> 00:00:18.077
about their emoji use
and see what they say.

00:00:21.057 --> 00:00:23.753
What is the emoji you use most often?

00:00:23.753 --> 00:00:25.848
- It's either the cry laughing emoji

00:00:25.858 --> 00:00:27.406
or it's like the little sassy lady.

00:00:27.406 --> 00:00:28.636
- [Voiceover] You mean the one behind you?

00:00:28.636 --> 00:00:29.906
- Ya, what?

00:00:29.906 --> 00:00:31.068
- It's this guy.

00:00:31.068 --> 00:00:33.065
- Definitely the tongue
sticking out emoji, like the--

00:00:34.035 --> 00:00:37.848
- The word of the year for 2015
is the crying laughing emoji

00:00:37.848 --> 00:00:39.066
do you agree?

00:00:39.066 --> 00:00:41.527
- No that's stupid it's
not a word, it's an emoji.

00:00:41.527 --> 00:00:43.246
- How is an emoji a word?

00:00:43.246 --> 00:00:44.393
- Are they words now?

00:00:44.393 --> 00:00:46.580
Is that where we are with life?

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:50.129
- Maybe, a picture is worth
a thousand of them so--

00:00:51.439 --> 00:00:53.396
- No (laughs).

00:00:53.396 --> 00:00:54.801
- That is so cool!

00:00:54.801 --> 00:00:56.908
That's fucking dope can you believe that?

00:00:56.908 --> 00:00:58.465
- I use that all the time,

00:00:58.465 --> 00:01:01.308
just for anything, both
positive and negative.

00:01:01.308 --> 00:01:03.071
- I think that's the
perfect emoji to be like,

00:01:03.671 --> 00:01:05.159
my life is so hard and I'm really stressed

00:01:05.159 --> 00:01:07.113
but at the same time
I'm laughing about it.

00:01:07.113 --> 00:01:09.392
- When you can communicate
like with your phone

00:01:09.392 --> 00:01:11.257
and through like pictures and stuff,

00:01:11.257 --> 00:01:13.416
it's pretty much created
like this like new language.

00:01:13.416 --> 00:01:15.112
- I don't think emojis should be words,

00:01:15.112 --> 00:01:16.887
I think that's a
dangerous road to go down.

00:01:16.887 --> 00:01:19.674
'Cause soon we'll just
be not communicating.

00:01:19.674 --> 00:01:21.114
We'll just be staring at each other.

00:01:21.114 --> 00:01:22.819
- Is that the only emoji that got in?

00:01:22.819 --> 00:01:23.819
- Mhm.

00:01:23.819 --> 00:01:25.247
That's not like even top ten emoji.

00:01:25.247 --> 00:01:26.675
Poop emoji should go in.

00:01:26.675 --> 00:01:28.210
Little chicken emoji,
what about the ghost?

00:01:28.210 --> 00:01:31.456
I think that people who are
using the crying laughing emoji

00:01:31.456 --> 00:01:34.536
are using it in lieu of actual humor

00:01:34.536 --> 00:01:35.823
and they are weak people.

00:01:37.233 --> 00:01:37.957
- Damn.

00:01:37.957 --> 00:01:39.820
- OK, OK, I have something to say to that.

00:01:39.820 --> 00:01:42.612
Crying laughing emoji,
number one, top emoji.

00:01:42.612 --> 00:01:43.891
Number one top emoji.

00:01:43.891 --> 00:01:46.122
- Yes, proves my point, proves my point.

00:01:46.122 --> 00:01:47.175
- Say I'm wrong, say I'm wrong.

00:01:47.175 --> 00:01:48.012
- You're wrong.

00:01:48.012 --> 00:01:49.092
- I'm right.

00:01:57.072 --> 00:01:58.727
- It's here! It's here!

00:01:58.727 --> 00:02:00.731
- [All] It's here!

00:02:00.731 --> 00:02:02.385
- [All] It's here!

00:02:02.385 --> 00:02:03.033
- Get it.

00:02:03.033 --> 00:02:03.708
- Get it.

00:02:03.708 --> 00:02:05.460
- There, get it.

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:06.934
- I think they got it, get it.

00:02:06.934 --> 00:02:08.025
- Ya you get it.

00:02:08.025 --> 00:02:08.942
- It's here.

